{"term":"provision","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:859234730e76edb9bd","definition":"An item of goods or supplies, especially food, obtained for future use.","example":"[H]e hath preſerued all points of Humanity, in taking Order, and making Proviſion for the Releefe of Strangers diſtreſſed; whereof you have taſted.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["alternative provision","improvision","make provision for","overprovision","preprovision","provisionary","provisioner","provisionless","provisionment","reprovision","spendthrift provision","sunrise provision","sunset provision","transitional provision","underprovision","unprovision"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/provision#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4035d515bf3b566127","definition":"The act of providing, or making previous preparation.","example":"Fiue dayes we do allot thee for prouision,\nTo shield thee from disasters of the world,","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["alternative provision","improvision","make provision for","overprovision","preprovision","provisionary","provisioner","provisionless","provisionment","reprovision","spendthrift provision","sunrise provision","sunset provision","transitional provision","underprovision","unprovision"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/provision#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e6f8a081e6623bb496","definition":"Money set aside for a future event.","example":"And as congressional Republicans were passing a very unpopular Trump agenda bill last month, Vice President JD Vance argued that its historic expansion of Immigration and Customs Enforcement and new immigration enforcement provisions were so important that “everything else” was “immaterial.”","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["alternative provision","improvision","make provision for","overprovision","preprovision","provisionary","provisioner","provisionless","provisionment","reprovision","spendthrift provision","sunrise provision","sunset provision","transitional provision","underprovision","unprovision"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/provision#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:25ad9e31651e281baf","definition":"A liability or contra account to recognise likely future adverse events associated with current transactions.","example":"We increased our provision for bad debts on credit sales going into the recession.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["alternative provision","improvision","make provision for","overprovision","preprovision","provisionary","provisioner","provisionless","provisionment","reprovision","spendthrift provision","sunrise provision","sunset provision","transitional provision","underprovision","unprovision"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/provision#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1c23415006456f0631","definition":"A clause in a legal instrument, a law, etc., providing for a particular matter; stipulation; proviso.","example":"An arrest shall be made in accordance with the provisions of this Act.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["condition","disposition","stipulation"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["alternative provision","improvision","make provision for","overprovision","preprovision","provisionary","provisioner","provisionless","provisionment","reprovision","spendthrift provision","sunrise provision","sunset provision","transitional provision","underprovision","unprovision"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/provision#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cb254d9b5147834b82","definition":"Regular induction into a benefice, comprehending nomination, collation, and installation.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["alternative provision","improvision","make provision for","overprovision","preprovision","provisionary","provisioner","provisionless","provisionment","reprovision","spendthrift provision","sunrise provision","sunset provision","transitional provision","underprovision","unprovision"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/provision#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e81de71bc92874ed90","definition":"A nomination by the pope to a benefice before it became vacant, depriving the patron of his right of presentation.","example":"a papal provision","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"UK, historical","register":"UK, countable, historical, uncountable","wordFamily":["alternative provision","improvision","make provision for","overprovision","preprovision","provisionary","provisioner","provisionless","provisionment","reprovision","spendthrift provision","sunrise provision","sunset provision","transitional provision","underprovision","unprovision"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/provision#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:03608e2fe7a6f27bb3","definition":"To supply with provisions.","example":"to provision an army","pos":"verb","synonyms":["supply","victual"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["alternative provision","improvision","make provision for","overprovision","preprovision","provisionary","provisioner","provisionless","provisionment","reprovision","spendthrift provision","sunrise provision","sunset provision","transitional provision","underprovision","unprovision","unprovisioned"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/provision#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1f4413270837ffa8ee","definition":"To supply (a user) with an account, resources, etc. so that they can use a system; to install the necessary software on a bare-bones system so it can be used for a specific purpose.","example":"A solution is to provision new systems on a private network where they can receive updates, patches, and secure configurations from an internal repository before being placed into a production network.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["supply","victual"],"antonyms":["deprovision"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["alternative provision","improvision","make provision for","overprovision","preprovision","provisionary","provisioner","provisionless","provisionment","reprovision","spendthrift provision","sunrise provision","sunset provision","transitional provision","underprovision","unprovision","unprovisioned"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/provision#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/pɹəˈvɪʒ.ən/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/44/En-us-provision.ogg/En-us-provision.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["alternative provision","improvision","make provision for","overprovision","preprovision","provisionary","provisioner","provisionle